<title>INDONESIA: Bakrie mulls link-up with Mexican firm.</title>
<headline>Bakrie mulls link-up with Mexican firm.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian conglomerate PT Bakrie &amp; Brothers said on Wednesday it was considering forming a joint-venture cement company with Mexico's Cementos de Mexico SA DE CV.</p>
<p>&quot;Bakrie is considering forming a joint-venture to build a cement plant in Indonesia, but it is all at the initial stage now,&quot; investor relation manager Suresh Kumar told Reuters.</p>
<p>Among prospective foreign partners was Mexico's cement firm Cementos de Mexico, he said. Kumar declined to give further details. -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
